2010-11-23  Salomon Eliasson  <s.eliasson@ltu.se>

	* atmlab-1-0-116

	* handy/catstruct.m (catstruct):
	A very useful function for merging structures:
	
	X = CATSTRUCT(S1,S2,S3,...) concates the structures S1, S2,
	... into one structure X.

	CATSTRUCT(S1,S2,'sorted') will sort the fieldnames alphabetically.

	If a fieldname occurs more than once in the argument list, only
	the last occurence is used, and the fields are alphabetically
	sorted.

	To sort the fieldnames of a structure A use: A =
	CATSTRUCT(A,'sorted') ;

	http://www.mathworks.com/matlabcentral/fileexchange/7842

